// 2D flat-plate cascade (Otsuka et al. 1996 baseline): beta = 15 deg, pitch d = 0.05 m, chord 3d.
// Blade-aligned coordinates: inflow at incidence alphaDeg to the blades (upward -> lower boundary
// bladeSS is the suction side). sigma = (p_inlet - pv)/(0.5 rho U^2) is imposed at the INLET by a feedback controller on the
// outlet pressure (v3): target inlet p holds at sigmaStart until tHold, ramps to sigma at tRamp.
// v1 (outlet p fixed) left inlet sigma uncontrolled (cascade raises p by 0.19-0.38 q);
// v2 (pressure inlet + flowRate outlet) diverged at 6 ms.
// Set sigma / alphaDeg with sed (never foamDictionary -set: it freezes the #eval values).
Uinf        10;
alphaDeg    5.0;
rhoL        999.19;
pSat        3169;
sigma       0.2;
sigmaStart  10.0;
tHold       0.03;
tRamp       0.08;
qInf        #eval{ 0.5*$rhoL*$Uinf*$Uinf };
pIn         #eval{ $pSat + $sigma*$qInf };
kGain       0.05;      // controller gain per corrector call
pStart      #eval{ $pSat + $sigmaStart*$qInf };
Ux          #eval{ $Uinf*cos(degToRad($alphaDeg)) };
Uy          #eval{ $Uinf*sin(degToRad($alphaDeg)) };
kIn         0.06;
omegaIn     64;
